  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Base and place value"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A number system is a way of representing numbers using a set of symbols. Its base (radix) is the number of symbols it uses. The value of each digit depends on its position: the place value is the base raised to the position, counting 0 for the digit just left of the point. Decimal has base 10 (0–9), binary base 2 (0, 1), octal base 8 (0–7) and hexadecimal base 16 (0–9 and A–F, where A = 10 … F = 15). A subscript shows the base, as in $(101)_2$."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Decimal: base 10, digits 0–9"
    },
    {
     "en": "Binary: base 2, digits 0 and 1 (bits)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Octal: base 8, digits 0–7"
    },
    {
     "en": "Hexadecimal: base 16, 0–9 and A–F"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A number system is a way of representing numbers using a set of symbols. Its base (radix) is the number of symbols it uses. The value of each digit depends on its position: the place value is the base raised to the position, counting 0 for the digit just left of the point. Decimal has base 10 (0–9), binary base 2 (0, 1), octal base 8 (0–7) and hexadecimal base 16 (0–9 and A–F, where A = 10 … F = 15). A subscript shows the base, as in $(101)_2$.",
    "kn": "ಸಂಖ್ಯಾ ಪದ್ಧತಿಯ ಆಧಾರ ಎಂದರೆ ಅದು ಬಳಸುವ ಚಿಹ್ನೆಗಳ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆ. ಅಂಕಿಯ ಮೌಲ್ಯ ಅದರ ಸ್ಥಾನವನ್ನು ಅವಲಂಬಿಸಿದೆ. ದಶಮಾನ ಆಧಾರ 10, ದ್ವಿಮಾನ ಆಧಾರ 2, ಅಷ್ಟಮಾನ ಆಧಾರ 8, ಷೋಡಶಮಾನ ಆಧಾರ 16 (0–9 ಮತ್ತು A–F)."
   },
   "formula": "N = d_{n-1}b^{n-1} + \\dots + d_1 b^1 + d_0 b^0 + d_{-1} b^{-1} + \\dots"
  },
