   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Why octal and hexadecimal?"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "Long binary strings are hard to read. One octal digit stands for exactly 3 bits and one hexadecimal digit for exactly 4 bits, so they are compact ways of writing binary. Hexadecimal is used for memory addresses, for MAC addresses of network cards, and for colour codes on web pages: #FF0000 is pure red because red = FF (255), green = 00 and blue = 00."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "1 octal digit = 3 bits"
    },
    {
     "en": "1 hex digit = 4 bits"
    },
    {
     "en": "Hex uses: memory addresses, MAC addresses, colour codes such as #FF0000"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Long binary strings are hard to read. One octal digit stands for exactly 3 bits and one hexadecimal digit for exactly 4 bits, so they are compact ways of writing binary. Hexadecimal is used for memory addresses, for MAC addresses of network cards, and for colour codes on web pages: #FF0000 is pure red because red = FF (255), green = 00 and blue = 00.",
    "kn": "ಉದ್ದದ ದ್ವಿಮಾನ ಸಂಖ್ಯೆಗಳನ್ನು ಓದುವುದು ಕಷ್ಟ. ಒಂದು ಅಷ್ಟಮಾನ ಅಂಕಿ 3 ಬಿಟ್‌ಗಳಿಗೆ, ಒಂದು ಷೋಡಶಮಾನ ಅಂಕಿ 4 ಬಿಟ್‌ಗಳಿಗೆ ಸಮ. ಷೋಡಶಮಾನವನ್ನು ಸ್ಮರಣೆ ವಿಳಾಸ, MAC ವಿಳಾಸ ಮತ್ತು ವೆಬ್ ಬಣ್ಣ ಸಂಕೇತಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಬಳಸುತ್ತಾರೆ."
